          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">232</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">6</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">a</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="12" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom">
              <div>
                <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">(19) In May 2025, before the planned closure of J.H. Campbell, the U.S. Secretary of Energy issued an emergency order under section 202(c) of the Federal Power Act requiring J.H. Campbell to continue operating for 90 days, through August 20, 2025. Subsequently, the U.S. Secretary of Energy issued three additional emergency orders for 90 days each, currently requiring continued operation of J.H. Campbell through May 18, 2026. These orders stated that continued operation of J.H. Campbell was required to meet an energy emergency across MISO&#8217;s North and Central regions. Consistent with the Federal Power Act and DOE regulations, the orders authorize Consumers to obtain cost recovery at FERC. The Company has recorded a regulatory asset reflecting costs associated with the continued operation of the J.H. Campbell facility. Consumers has also recorded an additional FERC Regulatory Asset for the expected plant depreciation, return on plant net book value, property tax and insurance, and return on fuel inventory that are expected to be approved for cost recovery at FERC. Recovery of these amounts is subject to regulatory review and approval.</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <span>
                  <br/>
                </span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents the financial impact of the U.S. Secretary of Energy emergency orders, offset by the amounts due to joint owners.</span>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="height:15pt">
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
